ld_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nVersion: v4.5.beta4.offical [2d113cc22]\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 10, Version: v4.5.beta4.offical [2d113cc22]\n\n### Issue description\n\nHi,\n\nWhen local_to_scene is set to true, typed Dictionary[int, CustomResource] data assigned in the inspector are not duplicated - they reset to their default value defined in the script. When local_to_scene is false, the values are preserved correctly.\n\nExpected behavior:\nTyped dictionary assigned in the inspector should be duplicated, regardless of local_to_scene setting.\n\n<img width=\"2558\" height=\"1401\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1613ec04-2252-42d1-8313-2ffacd1b4208\" />\n\n\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create new custom resource script (e.g. class_name MyCustomResource extends Resource)\n2. Create another custom resource script and define Typed Dictionary variable with reference to resource from step 1 (e.g. var dict: Dictionary[int, MyCustomResource])\n3. Add some entries to dict\n4. Create .tres and set local_to_scene  - TRUE\n5. Open new scene with node as root and define new variable of resource from step 2\n6. Print dict to console\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[typed-dictionary-local-to-scene.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21585741/typed-dictionary-local-to-scene.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.githu